p.src:
For a vector field $\mathbf A=(A_x,A_y,A_z)$, the scalar $\nabla\cdot\mathbf A
  =
  \frac{\partial A_x}{\partial x}
  +\frac{\partial A_y}{\partial y}
  +\frac{\partial A_z}{\partial z}$ is its divergence. In fluid language, positive divergence measures a local tendency to flow outward, while negative divergence measures a tendency to converge inward. A source of fluid produces positive divergence; a sink produces negative divergence. This picture is qualitative, but it will make the source-free character of the magnetic field transparent.

